<title>BAHRAIN: United Gulf Bank H1 net profit sharply up.</title>
<headline>United Gulf Bank H1 net profit sharply up.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-09-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>	    (million U.S. dollars unless stated)</p>
<p> Net profit		  5.22	 vs    0.18</p>
<p> Net operating income    6.88	 vs    0.497 loss</p>
<p> Shareholders' equity  225.17	 vs  221.38</p>
<p> Loans and advances     32.42	 vs   18.64</p>
<p> Assets		    355.54	 vs  440.04</p>
<p>Full Name: United Gulf Bank (B.S.C.) E.C.</p>
<p>Note - The Bahrain-based offshore investment bank is 97 percent owned by Kuwait Investment Projects Company.</p>
<p>The bank said the reduction in total assets had been in line with its strategy to book its profits in the managed portfolio, securities and real estate investments to reposition itself for new investment opportunities.</p>
</text>
